node CRL · CRL · ⟦CORAL:CRL:1340e6⟧

WHO   — CORAL — a life-science sphere — the brainless mind
WHAT  — A coral is two lives fused into one, repeated a billion times into a reef you can see from space. The animal — a tiny anemone-like polyp — shelters microscopic algae in its flesh; the algae feed it with sunlight. Together they build the largest living structures on Earth. And when the sea grows too warm, the partners break apart, and the reef turns white and starves.
WHERE — intelligence without a brain  Framework inputs: the living; the rule; the signal; the open question  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — A coral is two lives fused into one, repeated a billion times into a reef you can see from space. The animal — a tiny anemone-like polyp — shelters microscopic algae in its flesh; the algae feed it with sunlight. Together they build the largest living structures on Earth. And when the sea grows too warm, the partners break apart, and the reef turns white and starves.
HOW   — Crystallized from the public record of the science.

